WEBVTT

00:17.416 --> 00:20.790
Wash away my troubles
Wash away my pain…

00:20.791 --> 00:22.790
My family believes in giving back,

00:22.791 --> 00:26.790
so I couldn't be more proud to be opening
one of our helping hands, early learning,

00:26.791 --> 00:30.665
and outreach centers
right here in my hometown.

00:30.666 --> 00:35.207
Giving at-risk kids the support they need
in a safe and nurturing environment.

00:35.208 --> 00:38.790
So with that,
thank you so much for coming out.

00:38.791 --> 00:40.333
Please enjoy the evening.

00:45.250 --> 00:46.958
- What'd you think?
- It was great.

00:48.666 --> 00:50.625
What did you really think?

00:51.500 --> 00:52.666
How much time do we have?

00:55.541 --> 00:58.082
You go everywhere with a red pen
to look for things to correct?

00:58.083 --> 01:00.041
- Yes, I do.
- Seriously?

01:00.708 --> 01:02.999
You know what they say,
writing is rewriting.

01:03.000 --> 01:04.208
- Is it?
- It is.

01:05.458 --> 01:09.457
Rachel, this is a welcome speech, okay?
It's not an exposé for The Globe.

01:09.458 --> 01:11.624
You don't need to…
Hey, that was a good line.

01:11.625 --> 01:13.832
- I know, but it's gonna be better.
- Hey, you know what?

01:13.833 --> 01:16.749
- Stand down here. You're done.
- Just wait. No, please. No, no, no.

01:16.750 --> 01:18.666
I got it. I got it. Okay. Thank you.

01:23.708 --> 01:25.082
Hey, look at me.

01:25.083 --> 01:28.165
Your mom is gonna see the amazing work
that you've done here tonight.

01:28.166 --> 01:29.791
- I promise.
- I doubt it.

01:30.625 --> 01:32.541
She still just sees me as this…

01:33.875 --> 01:37.790
Spoiled playboy who once rented out
the entire club level at the Ritz

01:37.791 --> 01:40.249
to have a water balloon fight
with the Patriots cheerleaders?

01:40.250 --> 01:41.791
I think it was the Celtics.

01:42.875 --> 01:44.665
I'm not that guy anymore.

01:44.666 --> 01:46.749
- I'm not.
- I know.

01:46.750 --> 01:47.915
I just…

01:47.916 --> 01:50.665
We broke up, I got my shit together,

01:50.666 --> 01:53.208
I even started working
for my mother's foundation.

01:53.708 --> 01:55.499
You got me on a better path,

01:55.500 --> 01:58.666
but she just refuses to see it.

02:00.125 --> 02:01.124
And at some point,

02:01.125 --> 02:03.707
you have to start living your life
for you, Hayden, not for her.

02:03.708 --> 02:07.874
And, um, I just want the crowd here
to know that we didn't break up,

02:07.875 --> 02:09.375
you broke up with me.

02:10.125 --> 02:11.791
Biggest mistake of my life.

02:18.375 --> 02:19.916
Give me another shot.

02:26.125 --> 02:27.666
I don't wanna lose what we have.

02:30.500 --> 02:31.750
Wow.

02:32.791 --> 02:34.833
So that's what that feels like.

02:35.625 --> 02:36.583
What?

02:37.291 --> 02:38.791
Not getting what I want.

02:41.583 --> 02:42.666
Besides…

02:44.791 --> 02:48.458
this is the one meaningful relationship
where I hold all the cards.

02:51.500 --> 02:52.625
Come here.

02:53.666 --> 02:54.833
I'm proud of you.

03:02.750 --> 03:03.958
Where is she?

03:05.000 --> 03:06.125
Where's Rachel?

03:07.541 --> 03:09.040
Tell me, or I call the police.

03:09.041 --> 03:10.832
She was arrested by the FBI.

03:10.833 --> 03:12.333
Arrested by the FBI? How…

03:13.125 --> 03:14.790
How could you let that happen to her?

03:14.791 --> 03:16.166
It's not what I wanted.

03:17.375 --> 03:19.541
- Can I explain?
- You'll explain to the cops.

03:20.333 --> 03:21.583
My son's alive.

03:41.333 --> 03:44.707
The search for David Burroughs
continues in Lower Manhattan.

03:44.708 --> 03:49.000
They are pursuing every lead,
but so far, the fugitive remains at large.

03:51.458 --> 03:52.707
Hey.

03:52.708 --> 03:53.583
Hey.

03:55.125 --> 03:57.500
- Have you spoken to Hilde yet?
- No.

03:58.125 --> 04:00.333
EMTs are gonna come down,
tell us when it's okay to go up.

04:00.916 --> 04:03.165
By the way,
what did you want to talk to me about?

04:03.166 --> 04:05.458
- What do you mean?
- In the van.

04:06.625 --> 04:08.708
You tell me there was something
you wanted to talk to me about.

04:10.250 --> 04:12.458
Julie put me up to lead the FTF
out of Seattle.

04:14.291 --> 04:15.415
Well, that's great news.

04:15.416 --> 04:17.624
It would mean I'd have to move to Seattle.

04:17.625 --> 04:19.333
Be a hell of a commute if you didn't.

04:21.041 --> 04:21.875
What do you think?

04:23.458 --> 04:24.874
Agent Williams.

04:24.875 --> 04:26.666
They said you could talk to her now.

04:27.875 --> 04:31.833
Ms. Winslow, I'm Agent Max Williams.
This is my partner, Agent Greer.

04:32.833 --> 04:34.707
I know you've been through a lot tonight.

04:34.708 --> 04:37.541
You said I'd be protected,
and you let a madman hold me at gunpoint.

04:38.125 --> 04:41.665
Yeah, I'm sorry about that.
It must have been terrifying.

04:41.666 --> 04:42.999
It was.

04:43.000 --> 04:45.666
Did he tell you what he was doing here
or what this is about?

04:46.541 --> 04:47.458
No.

04:51.625 --> 04:53.416
I'm sorry. So…

04:54.416 --> 04:57.333
he broke in, and he held you at gunpoint,

04:58.416 --> 04:59.458
and he never said why?

05:00.291 --> 05:01.125
No.

05:02.250 --> 05:06.082
So he comes all the way to New York
to talk to you and doesn't say anything?

05:06.083 --> 05:07.875
Don't you find that a little odd?

05:08.583 --> 05:09.875
Know what else is odd?

05:10.791 --> 05:13.874
- He left his gun hanging behind.
- It all happened so fast.

05:13.875 --> 05:18.375
Well, it didn't happen that fast, right?
He was in your house for ten minutes?

05:22.916 --> 05:24.208
Ms. Winslow…

05:27.291 --> 05:28.708
why are you lying to us?

05:31.416 --> 05:33.125
- I-I'm not.
- No?

05:34.833 --> 05:38.415
You said you would keep me safe,
and now you're treating me like a suspect.

05:38.416 --> 05:40.416
The fire escape
that Burroughs used to get away,

05:41.166 --> 05:43.415
the one that's off your bedroom window,

05:43.416 --> 05:45.541
you can't see it from your living room.

05:46.375 --> 05:47.708
How did he know it was there?

05:48.791 --> 05:49.958
Lucky guess.

05:51.416 --> 05:52.708
Right?

05:58.458 --> 06:01.665
She helped him escape.
Why is she protecting him?

06:01.666 --> 06:02.624
Why do you think?

06:02.625 --> 06:04.499
We're looking at this all wrong.

06:04.500 --> 06:06.707
If Burroughs didn't come here for revenge…

06:06.708 --> 06:08.875
Then what did he come here for?

06:12.416 --> 06:13.458
So,

06:14.541 --> 06:16.999
this Hilde lady, she lies on the stand.

06:17.000 --> 06:19.790
That's grounds for retrial, isn't it?
Why don't you just take that to the cops?

06:19.791 --> 06:21.415
If the kidnappers know
that the cops are involved,

06:21.416 --> 06:22.790
who knows what they're gonna do?

06:22.791 --> 06:25.625
And by kidnappers,
you mean the Boston mob.

06:27.458 --> 06:29.540
I don't need you to believe me.
I need you to help Rachel.

06:29.541 --> 06:31.124
Of course I will, you know that.

06:31.125 --> 06:33.332
- That's not the question.
- Mm-hmm. What is?

06:33.333 --> 06:37.958
Even if I could get her out,
and it's a big if, what then, huh?

06:38.583 --> 06:41.874
If she's seen helping you,
she's-- She's just gonna end up in prison.

06:41.875 --> 06:44.582
- I'll keep her out of it.
- Good luck with that.

06:44.583 --> 06:47.915
The minute she gets
her sights set on something, that's it.

06:47.916 --> 06:50.916
It won't matter. Hilde said
that she's gonna help me tomorrow.

06:52.666 --> 06:55.583
I need you to call Skunk and get him
to come to New York. Can you do that?

06:57.708 --> 06:59.916
After that, you'll never see me again.

07:00.583 --> 07:03.500
Get Rachel out, tell her I said thank you,
and I'll find Matthew on my own.

07:04.416 --> 07:05.250
Wait.

07:08.791 --> 07:10.708
Where are you gonna stay tonight?

07:11.291 --> 07:13.957
- I don't know, work it out.
- You're a wanted fugitive, David.

07:13.958 --> 07:16.915
I don't think you're gonna have
many options. I mean, you…

07:16.916 --> 07:18.540
you're already here.

07:18.541 --> 07:19.832
You sure?

07:19.833 --> 07:22.000
No. Not even.

07:22.708 --> 07:24.457
But when I see Rachel tomorrow,

07:24.458 --> 07:27.291
I can't very well tell her
that I kicked you out, can I?

07:38.000 --> 07:39.291
This is a waste of time.

07:41.125 --> 07:43.665
- The cops went over all this.
- Cops thought he did it.

07:43.666 --> 07:46.250
They focused on him from the beginning.
You know how that plays out.

07:46.833 --> 07:49.665
There's gotta be some unanswered question,
some loose end

07:49.666 --> 07:51.875
that they didn't think
was important at the time.

07:52.875 --> 07:56.999
On the night of Matthew's abduction,
Cheryl was working at the hospital, right?

07:57.000 --> 07:59.582
She got called in for a bus accident.

07:59.583 --> 08:02.666
That's just it.
There's no accident report in the file.

08:03.291 --> 08:07.499
Well, it got misplaced,
or they lost it when they boxed it up.

08:07.500 --> 08:11.207
Agreed, but in a world of loose ends
and unanswered questions…

08:11.208 --> 08:13.666
I had a friend at the MTA.
I'm gonna call him and see what he says.

08:19.500 --> 08:20.750
You all right?

08:21.333 --> 08:23.708
- Should have done more.
- Like what?

08:25.583 --> 08:26.916
Believe him, for starters.

08:30.625 --> 08:32.666
I need to see my boy again, Philip.

08:38.250 --> 08:39.666
Appreciate your help.

08:41.833 --> 08:45.124
You're not gonna believe this.
My friend checked the DOT database.

08:45.125 --> 08:48.249
The reason there's
no accident report in the file

08:48.250 --> 08:50.499
is because there was
no bus accident that night.

08:50.500 --> 08:52.290
No, not possible.

08:52.291 --> 08:54.249
Detectives would've
verified Cheryl's story.

08:54.250 --> 08:55.541
They did.

08:56.666 --> 09:00.958
The detectives spoke to a…
a hospital administrator. Yeah, here.

09:02.000 --> 09:03.583
He confirmed

09:04.208 --> 09:08.166
Cheryl was called into the hospital
that night due to a bus accident.

09:09.416 --> 09:10.749
Ronald Dreason.

09:10.750 --> 09:12.583
Cheryl's new husband.

09:14.541 --> 09:16.541
- Adam and I will go talk to him.
- No.

09:17.875 --> 09:18.875
I'll do it.

09:26.958 --> 09:28.625
I need you to listen to me.

09:29.708 --> 09:31.083
It's about Matthew.

09:32.291 --> 09:33.583
We think he's alive.

09:34.750 --> 09:37.540
Dr. Dreason. How's it going?

09:37.541 --> 09:40.165
Any chance I can convince you
to join me on rounds?

09:40.166 --> 09:41.458
Sure, why not?

09:42.166 --> 09:45.832
Obstetrics and pediatric surgery
often go hand in hand.

09:45.833 --> 09:50.332
Having someone of Dr. Dreason's
considerable talents is one of the reasons

09:50.333 --> 09:53.957
why I chose Boston General
when I left the private sector.

09:53.958 --> 09:56.207
It wasn't for the long hours
and mounds of paperwork?

09:56.208 --> 09:57.832
That's just a bonus.

09:57.833 --> 09:59.874
Why don't we start in pediatrics
since we have you?

09:59.875 --> 10:00.875
Sounds good.

10:06.625 --> 10:08.790
Cheryl, you okay?

10:08.791 --> 10:13.374
Yeah, uh, I just need a minute.
Start without me. I'll catch up.

10:13.375 --> 10:14.749
Can I help you?

10:14.750 --> 10:17.457
Could you point me
toward Ronald Dreason's office?

10:17.458 --> 10:19.083
I'm sorry, he's not in today.

10:19.583 --> 10:20.458
Lenny?

10:26.208 --> 10:27.208
Congratulations.

10:28.541 --> 10:29.666
Thank you.

10:30.875 --> 10:31.916
Boy or girl?

10:33.000 --> 10:34.000
It's a girl.

10:38.958 --> 10:39.958
When were you diagnosed?

10:42.583 --> 10:44.541
Those warts can be itchy.

10:46.375 --> 10:47.708
How are you holding up?

10:49.041 --> 10:50.166
I'm fine.

10:51.625 --> 10:53.083
The Burroughs' motto.

10:56.000 --> 10:57.500
Why are you here?

10:58.916 --> 11:01.125
I think I know
why David broke out of prison.

11:01.750 --> 11:03.541
Yeah, me too.

11:04.041 --> 11:04.875
Rachel called.

11:08.291 --> 11:09.958
Matthew's gone, Lenny.

11:12.041 --> 11:14.166
Nothing we can do will change that.

11:15.291 --> 11:17.375
Yeah, you're probably right. But, uh…

11:18.250 --> 11:22.250
if you'll indulge an old man
a few questions, it would mean a lot.

11:23.041 --> 11:24.000
Go ahead.

11:24.625 --> 11:28.082
That night you were brought down
to the hospital for a bus accident.

11:28.083 --> 11:29.083
Mm-hmm.

11:29.750 --> 11:32.999
- What happened when you got here?
- What do you mean?

11:33.000 --> 11:34.790
Did you treat the victims?

11:34.791 --> 11:40.125
No, uh, the accident had been rerouted
to a different hospital.

11:40.958 --> 11:42.416
Who told you that?

11:43.000 --> 11:44.500
The hospital administrator.

11:45.500 --> 11:47.916
- Ronald?
- Yes, Ronald.

11:48.625 --> 11:49.707
What does it matter?

11:49.708 --> 11:54.000
It matters because there were
no bus accidents that night, Cheryl.

11:54.958 --> 11:56.916
- Of course there was.
- No.

11:57.583 --> 11:58.749
According to the MTA,

11:58.750 --> 12:02.291
there were no bus accidents
in the Greater Boston Area that night.

12:03.000 --> 12:05.833
That, um… That doesn't make any sense.

12:06.625 --> 12:10.166
I agree. That's why I want
to talk to Ronald about it.

12:11.625 --> 12:13.749
What are you implying here, Lenny?

12:13.750 --> 12:17.791
That my husband made up a bus accident
to get me to the hospital? Is--

12:18.750 --> 12:20.625
Do you know how absurd that sounds?

12:23.250 --> 12:24.250
Yeah.

12:25.375 --> 12:26.375
You're right.

12:27.625 --> 12:29.000
I shouldn't have come.

12:31.583 --> 12:32.666
It was good to see you.

12:39.416 --> 12:40.625
I'm happy for you.

12:42.375 --> 12:43.375
I really am.

13:00.125 --> 13:02.707
You've reached
Ronald Dreason of Boston General.

13:02.708 --> 13:03.832
Leave a message.

13:03.833 --> 13:07.375
I need to talk to you. Will you call me
back as soon as you get this?

13:13.833 --> 13:15.541
You never struck me as a gun guy.

13:16.125 --> 13:18.207
My mother's a bit of a worrier.

13:18.208 --> 13:20.999
Always felt better knowing
that I had a gun in the apartment.

13:21.000 --> 13:23.374
- You know how to handle one?
- Yeah, my dad's a cop.

13:23.375 --> 13:26.291
- You're not gonna shoot anybody, right?
- Well, that's the plan.

13:26.958 --> 13:31.125
- Still, this could come back on you.
- If it does, I'll just say it was stolen.

13:32.500 --> 13:35.125
Here. Take it before I change my mind.

13:37.041 --> 13:39.208
Hate to press my luck,
but can you drop me somewhere?

13:41.041 --> 13:42.458
Anything else?

13:53.333 --> 13:54.708
We have a problem.

14:12.000 --> 14:13.250
Take a look at this.

14:16.375 --> 14:19.208
A woman with her daughters
at an amusement park?

14:21.291 --> 14:23.082
Is this another way for you to remind me

14:23.083 --> 14:25.791
that I should've taken you more places
when you were a little kid?

14:27.208 --> 14:29.957
Rachel Mills was carrying it
around with her.

14:29.958 --> 14:31.500
Maybe it means something.

14:32.125 --> 14:34.000
And yes, you should have.

14:37.916 --> 14:40.083
I pulled Hilde's phone records.

14:41.458 --> 14:43.665
Yesterday, she made a call
to a Boston number,

14:43.666 --> 14:45.790
Kyle Bergin, a career scumbag.

14:45.791 --> 14:47.582
Capo for the Fisher family.

14:47.583 --> 14:50.749
Kyle Bergin, aka Skunk.

14:50.750 --> 14:53.874
Armed robbery, multiple assaults,
racketeering, extortion.

14:53.875 --> 14:55.540
What, was this guy born mobbed up?

14:55.541 --> 14:58.082
He also had a couple murder charges.

14:58.083 --> 15:00.249
They were tossed due to technicality.

15:00.250 --> 15:03.749
So, what is Hilde doing
calling someone like this?

15:03.750 --> 15:05.457
No idea. BPD is picking him up,

15:05.458 --> 15:07.957
and I'm having Hilde
brought down here so we can ask her.

15:07.958 --> 15:10.165
In the meantime,
I'm gonna take a last run at Rachel Mills

15:10.166 --> 15:11.707
before she's transferred to county.

15:11.708 --> 15:12.749
All right.

15:12.750 --> 15:16.040
And not for nothing, we all went
to Disneyland when you were nine.

15:16.041 --> 15:18.040
No, Mom and I went to Disneyland.

15:18.041 --> 15:21.540
You got as far as the hotel before
you caught a case and flew to Arizona.

15:21.541 --> 15:24.165
Oh, right. Yeah, the Browning escape.

15:24.166 --> 15:26.707
Well, we caught him
just outside of Phoenix.

15:26.708 --> 15:27.958
It was Tucson.

15:31.416 --> 15:33.791
I told David to meet me
at Washington Square Park.

15:36.375 --> 15:38.665
- What did you say?
- That I have answers for him.

15:38.666 --> 15:40.790
- You better hope he shows up.
- He will.

15:40.791 --> 15:43.500
Please tell Mr. Fisher
I did the right thing.

15:46.666 --> 15:47.875
Ms. Mills.

15:49.416 --> 15:50.583
How was your night?

15:51.208 --> 15:52.208
Pretty great.

15:53.000 --> 15:55.999
You guys should Airbnb this place
when you're not using it.

15:56.000 --> 15:56.916
Ha!

15:57.833 --> 15:58.790
That's cute.

15:58.791 --> 16:02.207
Sense of humor's key when you're looking
at 25 to life in prison.

16:02.208 --> 16:04.582
Speaking of which,
I brought something for you.

16:04.583 --> 16:07.208
Thought you might want it
for your new cell.

16:11.250 --> 16:13.083
You wanna tell me who's in the photo?

16:15.416 --> 16:16.874
Just some friends of mine.

16:16.875 --> 16:17.875
Okay.

16:18.750 --> 16:19.916
Should I tell her?

16:21.291 --> 16:23.832
We spoke to Hilde Winslow
after David paid her a visit.

16:23.833 --> 16:26.250
She wouldn't speak to us,
but know who she called when he left?

16:27.500 --> 16:30.875
A capo in the Fisher crime family.

16:35.250 --> 16:36.165
What's up?

16:36.166 --> 16:39.040
So, BPD couldn't find Kyle Bergin,
so they asked us to ping his phone.

16:39.041 --> 16:40.874
- Great. Where is he?
- He's here in the city.

16:40.875 --> 16:41.790
What are you talking about?

16:41.791 --> 16:44.999
Cell tower puts him
at Washington Square Park ten minutes ago,

16:45.000 --> 16:46.833
and Hilde Winslow is missing.

16:50.333 --> 16:52.832
That capo Hilde called
is named Kyle Bergin.

16:52.833 --> 16:54.541
That name mean anything to you?

16:55.125 --> 16:56.875
Goes by the nickname Skunk.

16:58.666 --> 16:59.625
I've never heard of him.

17:02.416 --> 17:04.291
Let me explain something to you.

17:05.333 --> 17:10.332
Kyle Bergin is a problem solver
for Nicky Fisher himself.

17:10.333 --> 17:13.541
Now, if he catches up with David
before we do, it's not going to end well.

17:14.166 --> 17:16.082
Rachel, if you really wanna protect David,

17:16.083 --> 17:18.083
you gotta tell us
where he is before it's too late.

17:22.458 --> 17:24.957
You know what? Fine. Call NYPD.

17:24.958 --> 17:26.874
I want Bergin picked up at the park.

17:26.875 --> 17:30.291
And put that one on a bus to MCC!

18:24.041 --> 18:25.208
Looking for someone?

18:25.875 --> 18:26.833
David Burroughs.

18:27.416 --> 18:29.000
Let's go, Skunk. Nice and easy.

18:31.291 --> 18:33.082
You had the old bird set me up.

18:33.083 --> 18:34.624
You know, I'm almost
a little bit impressed.

18:34.625 --> 18:36.874
You were such
a little bitch in high school.

18:36.875 --> 18:39.124
- Shut up.
- Always had Mackenzie fight for you.

18:39.125 --> 18:41.290
- Keep going.
- Hey, take it easy, tough guy.

18:41.291 --> 18:42.708
I'm just busting balls.

20:06.041 --> 20:07.083
Get up.

20:09.458 --> 20:11.957
Officers were on the way
when the shooting went down.

20:11.958 --> 20:15.207
Multiple witnesses say they saw Burroughs
arguing with another man

20:15.208 --> 20:16.790
before shots were fired.

20:16.791 --> 20:18.166
It's gotta be Skunk.

20:27.916 --> 20:28.875
Hilde Winslow.

20:30.083 --> 20:32.124
Driver's license read Harriet Winchester.

20:32.125 --> 20:34.499
- It's a long story.
- Which one of them shot her? Do we know?

20:34.500 --> 20:37.374
No, but we got a cell phone video
that was taken right after she was killed.

20:37.375 --> 20:38.957
- Let's see it.
- Officer.

20:38.958 --> 20:40.665
So Hilde helps Burroughs escape,

20:40.666 --> 20:43.999
then she calls Bergin,
and the three of them end up here.

20:44.000 --> 20:45.708
And then one of them shoots her?

20:46.916 --> 20:49.874
If Burroughs wanted her dead,
he would've killed her yesterday.

20:49.875 --> 20:52.708
If it was Bergin, the order definitely
came from Nicky Fisher.

20:53.541 --> 20:55.333
So how does Fisher fit into all of this?

20:56.000 --> 20:57.333
Here's the cell phone footage.

21:07.166 --> 21:08.416
Hmm.

21:11.125 --> 21:13.665
- Do we know which way Burroughs went?
- He ran south on Thompson.

21:13.666 --> 21:14.791
Chasing the other guy.

21:17.875 --> 21:20.624
Call MTA right now. Shut down the subways.

21:20.625 --> 21:21.541
What?

21:22.041 --> 21:25.999
After the gun went off, Skunk could've
shot Burroughs, but he didn't. Why?

21:26.000 --> 21:27.374
He just ran off.

21:27.375 --> 21:28.625
Hmm.

21:35.083 --> 21:36.000
That's blood.

21:40.000 --> 21:41.083
Skunk's been shot.

21:42.458 --> 21:44.541
If that's true, he won't get far.

21:51.583 --> 21:52.833
You're a dead man, Burroughs.

21:55.125 --> 21:56.875
I think you got us confused.

21:58.583 --> 21:59.708
Let me have a look.

22:01.208 --> 22:02.583
My wife is a doctor.

22:03.666 --> 22:04.958
Ex-wife.

22:05.541 --> 22:07.875
Gunshot like that,
you're probably going into shock.

22:08.500 --> 22:10.416
Now, I can get you an ambulance…

22:11.666 --> 22:13.083
if you tell me where my son is.

22:14.666 --> 22:16.541
Revere Cemetery.

22:36.625 --> 22:40.082
Rachel Mills,
JPATS to Metropolitan Corrections.

22:40.083 --> 22:40.958
Chopra!

22:41.666 --> 22:42.750
Hold up.

22:43.375 --> 22:44.457
Her lawyer's here.

22:44.458 --> 22:47.333
What? No. When did you make a phone call?

22:48.500 --> 22:49.500
I didn't.

22:57.458 --> 23:00.332
I don't mean to sound ungrateful,
but who are you and what just happened?

23:00.333 --> 23:03.374
I'm your lawyer. I managed to get you
released on a million-dollar bond,

23:03.375 --> 23:05.832
pending an evidentiary hearing
of insufficient evidence,

23:05.833 --> 23:08.416
improper procedure, and lack of cause.

23:09.083 --> 23:11.790
So I'm… free?

23:11.791 --> 23:13.040
Hardly.

23:13.041 --> 23:15.707
You're in a whole world of trouble,
just not today.

23:15.708 --> 23:18.040
Okay, well, you know
I don't have a million dollars, right?

23:18.041 --> 23:19.958
Yes, I gathered that.

23:20.583 --> 23:21.750
So…

23:31.416 --> 23:32.458
Why am I not surprised?

23:33.708 --> 23:36.374
Whenever I really need you, there you are.

23:36.375 --> 23:37.707
What can I say?

23:37.708 --> 23:42.249
I'm like your own personal, wealthy,
incredibly handsome guardian angel.

23:42.250 --> 23:43.707
You left out humble.

23:43.708 --> 23:45.291
Add it to the list.

23:50.333 --> 23:52.374
Wait, so how'd you know I'd been arrested?

23:52.375 --> 23:54.124
Well, I went home to check on you,

23:54.125 --> 23:58.082
and I found David,
wearing one of my suits, I might add.

23:58.083 --> 23:59.165
He's innocent.

23:59.166 --> 24:01.958
Even if he is, it's not
a "get out of jail free" card.

24:02.750 --> 24:05.165
Look, you get caught with David,

24:05.166 --> 24:07.707
there's no lawyer in the world
that's gonna be able to help you.

24:07.708 --> 24:10.582
- I can't worry about that right now.
- You should.

24:10.583 --> 24:12.082
You need to walk away.

24:12.083 --> 24:16.416
I know, look, do you remember that guy
named Skunk who grew up with David?

24:17.291 --> 24:18.249
Okay.

24:18.250 --> 24:20.457
We saw him at the Fourth of July party.

24:20.458 --> 24:24.541
He works for Nicky Fisher,
and he's here in New York to kill David.

24:25.750 --> 24:26.874
What are you talking about?

24:26.875 --> 24:29.458
I know, it's a long story,
but I have to find him.

24:30.041 --> 24:31.291
I have to find David.

24:32.875 --> 24:34.040
What?

24:34.041 --> 24:36.582
I dropped David off
just before I came to get you.

24:36.583 --> 24:37.583
Where?

24:39.000 --> 24:42.291
Hayden, come on, please.

24:45.666 --> 24:48.540
Skunk will wanna get
off the street and hole up somewhere.

24:48.541 --> 24:50.499
Well, the guy's leaking blood.

24:50.500 --> 24:54.499
It's not like he can just duck into a bar
or a restaurant and wait us out.

24:54.500 --> 24:57.415
Hey, Glenn. That's Glenn from
the Department of Transportation.

24:57.416 --> 24:59.040
You said there was
construction in the area.

24:59.041 --> 25:02.582
A stretch of paving on Mercer,
scaffolding on 8th,

25:02.583 --> 25:05.916
and an office renovation
on Thompson and Prince.

25:06.458 --> 25:08.540
Office renovation.
Are there crews there now?

25:08.541 --> 25:12.208
No. They ran into coding violations.
It's on hold.

25:13.000 --> 25:14.291
So the building's empty.

25:14.875 --> 25:16.666
Call tactical.
Have them meet us over there.

25:21.708 --> 25:24.750
You have no idea
what hell I've lived through.

25:26.291 --> 25:27.833
Or what I'm capable of.

25:28.583 --> 25:29.958
I'm gonna ask nicely.

25:30.708 --> 25:32.708
Why would Nicky take my son?

25:35.208 --> 25:39.874
Is this what you wanna be? You wanna
protect a man that kidnaps little kids?

25:39.875 --> 25:41.750
I thought you pieces of shit had a code.

25:44.208 --> 25:47.916
Tell me why Nicky Fisher took my son.

25:48.666 --> 25:50.374
I don't even know him.

25:50.375 --> 25:51.415
Tell me!

25:51.416 --> 25:53.291
Ask your father.

25:57.958 --> 25:59.208
What does that mean?

26:00.458 --> 26:01.416
You heard me.

26:02.083 --> 26:05.833
You wanna know what Nicky Fisher
might have against you and your family?

26:06.958 --> 26:08.583
Ask your old man.

26:10.291 --> 26:11.208
Ask him--

26:14.208 --> 26:15.833
Time's up, Burroughs.

26:16.500 --> 26:18.125
Even if you make it out,

26:19.000 --> 26:22.041
you ain't gonna last long walking around.

26:25.958 --> 26:28.875
You recognize any of the agents
that arrested you?

26:29.416 --> 26:30.625
Not yet.

26:32.875 --> 26:34.250
Shit. The coroner's here.

26:37.000 --> 26:38.291
Give me your phone.

26:46.958 --> 26:49.791
The whole world wants you dead, Burroughs.

26:50.458 --> 26:52.291
Not just me.

26:53.416 --> 26:55.582
- Rachel?
- David, thank God.

26:55.583 --> 26:57.082
I'm here with Hayden. Where are you?

26:57.083 --> 26:59.749
I'm in an empty building two blocks south
of the park. There's cops everywhere.

26:59.750 --> 27:02.249
- I don't think I can get out.
- All right, we're on our way.

27:02.250 --> 27:05.415
I'm heading to an alleyway
with a bunch of construction equipment.

27:05.416 --> 27:06.957
Wait, we passed the renovation
a couple blocks back.

27:06.958 --> 27:09.124
Hey, meet us at the corner
of Thompson and Prince.

27:09.125 --> 27:10.125
Got it.

27:23.291 --> 27:24.750
They're here.

28:01.291 --> 28:02.125
On your left.

28:07.750 --> 28:09.958
You on the ground! Put your hands up!

28:11.791 --> 28:13.083
Do it now, Bergin!

28:15.958 --> 28:16.916
No sign of Burroughs.

28:25.125 --> 28:26.458
First floor clear!

28:29.000 --> 28:31.290
Burroughs isn't here.
I need an ambulance up here right now.

28:31.291 --> 28:33.707
I want street closures
for a two-block radius.

28:33.708 --> 28:36.165
I want this entire area shut down.

28:36.166 --> 28:37.665
Roger that.

28:37.666 --> 28:38.583
He's gotta be close.

28:58.833 --> 29:00.624
- There he is.
- Got him.

29:00.625 --> 29:01.750
Hayden! Cops!

29:08.333 --> 29:11.749
Officers, I saw an armed man
over on Broadway!

29:11.750 --> 29:15.250
238 to Dispatch.
Suspect spotted on Broadway. Let's go.

29:17.208 --> 29:18.333
We're on the way.

29:24.916 --> 29:25.916
Hey.

29:33.791 --> 29:35.415
You spoke to Gerry?

29:35.416 --> 29:38.041
Yeah. She'll be here any minute.

29:40.791 --> 29:41.750
What about Briggs?

29:43.416 --> 29:45.041
I doubt I'll be going back.

29:45.583 --> 29:47.625
At least, not as the warden.

29:50.958 --> 29:52.583
I'm not sure I thanked you

29:53.583 --> 29:55.166
for what you did for David.

29:56.208 --> 29:58.708
I was thinking
about retiring early anyway.

29:59.541 --> 30:02.125
I know someone who'll be glad
you have more time on your hands.

30:03.041 --> 30:04.707
Pretty sure that ship has sailed.

30:04.708 --> 30:07.040
- I don't think Sophie would agree.
- No?

30:07.041 --> 30:09.915
Plus, she'll need a shoulder to cry on
when I'm dead and gone.

30:09.916 --> 30:11.541
Jesus, Lenny.

30:12.125 --> 30:14.374
- Hey.
- Well, look at this.

30:14.375 --> 30:16.458
- It's a real Revere PD reunion.
- Yeah.

30:17.833 --> 30:19.708
You look like hammered shit, Burroughs.

30:20.291 --> 30:21.291
Yeah.

30:22.166 --> 30:23.125
Cancer will do that.

30:24.625 --> 30:27.040
You didn't think to mention that
when you called?

30:27.041 --> 30:28.208
Lenny has cancer.

30:28.875 --> 30:30.000
Asshole.

30:30.666 --> 30:31.915
Sorry, Burroughs.

30:31.916 --> 30:33.915
No. How's the PI trade?

30:33.916 --> 30:35.166
Oh, you know.

30:35.958 --> 30:38.332
Fraud, infidelity,
people screwing each other over.

30:38.333 --> 30:40.165
It's a recession-proof business.

30:40.166 --> 30:42.332
A lot less paperwork
when you're not police too.

30:42.333 --> 30:44.124
Thanks for looking
into this for us, Gerry.

30:44.125 --> 30:46.375
All right, what do we got on this guy?

30:46.958 --> 30:48.624
Ronald Dreason.

30:48.625 --> 30:49.540
Yeah.

30:49.541 --> 30:53.457
No criminal record.
No civil action, lawsuits.

30:53.458 --> 30:54.750
He's a Boy Scout.

30:55.666 --> 30:58.499
Only time he crossed with law enforcement
was six years ago

30:58.500 --> 31:01.874
when his hospital was targeted by the feds
for a Medicare fraud ring.

31:01.875 --> 31:04.207
You know, fake patients,
phony billing, that sort of thing.

31:04.208 --> 31:06.415
So Ronald Dreason
was involved in Medicare fraud?

31:06.416 --> 31:10.124
No, he was the key witness against
the guy the feds believed was behind it.

31:10.125 --> 31:13.582
Only before it went to trial,
he got amnesia, refused to cooperate.

31:13.583 --> 31:14.832
Somebody got to him.

31:14.833 --> 31:16.958
So who'd the feds think was behind it?

31:17.833 --> 31:19.541
Nicky Fisher.

31:23.750 --> 31:25.625
You guys wanna tell me what's going on?

31:28.333 --> 31:30.458
All right. Well, if you change your mind,

31:31.083 --> 31:33.958
I'll be over there at the bar
drinking on your dime.

31:38.000 --> 31:39.374
Jesus, Lenny.

31:39.375 --> 31:42.499
What if Nicky is behind
Ronald placing that call?

31:42.500 --> 31:45.957
Makes up that fake bus accident that night
to get Cheryl out of the house.

31:45.958 --> 31:48.208
What if he's involved
in what happened to Matthew?

31:48.958 --> 31:50.041
Why would he do that?

31:51.375 --> 31:52.833
We both know why.

32:03.958 --> 32:05.041
Hello!

32:06.333 --> 32:07.583
Where have you been?

32:08.458 --> 32:09.500
I left you three messages.

32:10.500 --> 32:13.291
Sorry, I had my phone off
for the conference. What's going on?

32:14.041 --> 32:16.249
Lenny Burroughs
was at the hospital looking for you.

32:16.250 --> 32:17.665
For me? Why?

32:17.666 --> 32:20.833
He said there was no bus accident
the night Matthew was killed.

32:21.333 --> 32:22.458
He said you made it up.

32:23.500 --> 32:24.665
Why would I do that?

32:24.666 --> 32:27.541
I have no idea. But why would he say that?

32:28.875 --> 32:29.915
I'll give him a call.

32:29.916 --> 32:31.749
Whatever this is about,
there's gotta be a logical explanation.

32:31.750 --> 32:33.250
Yeah, you'd hope so.

32:37.166 --> 32:38.582
- I'm gonna shower.
- All right.

32:38.583 --> 32:39.458
Okay.

32:49.208 --> 32:51.208
Wait. He said, "Ask your father"?

32:51.791 --> 32:53.332
Yeah, it doesn't make sense.

32:53.333 --> 32:55.082
Sorry, don't mean to be the asshole,

32:55.083 --> 32:58.416
but I think the implication
is pretty clear, whether it's true or not.

32:59.625 --> 33:01.707
He's right. I gotta get the bus,
then I gotta talk to him.

33:01.708 --> 33:04.791
But the FBI knows my car,
and public transportation is out.

33:13.041 --> 33:13.958
Okay, here.

33:15.375 --> 33:16.541
Take it.

33:19.041 --> 33:20.875
- You sure?
- Take it.

33:23.333 --> 33:25.166
- Thank you.
- Yeah.

33:28.833 --> 33:31.500
You were supposed to leave.
That was the deal.

33:32.375 --> 33:33.708
- Well, things change.
- Do they?

33:34.291 --> 33:36.540
She's trying to help me find Matthew.
You can see that, right?

33:36.541 --> 33:40.833
At what cost, huh? Have you ever stopped
to think about that, about her?

33:42.833 --> 33:44.375
No. I didn't think so.

33:48.958 --> 33:50.665
Hey, Jim, can't really talk right now.

33:50.666 --> 33:54.415
You okay? I got a tip
that you've been arrested by the FBI.

33:54.416 --> 33:57.582
Yeah, aiding and abetting a fugitive
and accessory to murder.

33:57.583 --> 33:59.290
Don't worry, we didn't kill anyone.

33:59.291 --> 34:01.041
Oh. Well, then you're all good.

34:01.625 --> 34:03.582
Hey, can I call you later?
We've gotta get to Boston.

34:03.583 --> 34:06.166
What's in Boston?
Anything I can do to help?

34:07.958 --> 34:11.957
Okay, I appreciate everything
you've done. Seriously, thank you.

34:11.958 --> 34:14.665
But we both know why you're calling,
and the answer is no.

34:14.666 --> 34:18.415
Rachel, I've talked to my publisher.
He wants this story.

34:18.416 --> 34:19.499
Jim, you don't understand.

34:19.500 --> 34:22.290
If this story goes national,
it could put Matthew in danger.

34:22.291 --> 34:25.082
This story is going to go national.

34:25.083 --> 34:27.458
It's just a matter of when
and who breaks it.

34:29.083 --> 34:30.000
It won't be me.

34:31.083 --> 34:32.083
I gotta go.

34:37.166 --> 34:40.832
Chopra said some high-priced attorney
got Rachel Mills out on bail.

34:40.833 --> 34:41.875
What?!

34:42.458 --> 34:44.082
What judge would sign off on that?

34:44.083 --> 34:47.457
She was ID'd with Burroughs
right after that prison guard was killed.

34:47.458 --> 34:49.415
- That's accessory to murder.
- Not anymore.

34:49.416 --> 34:51.999
GSR came back positive on Wesson.
M.E. is ruling it a suicide.

34:52.000 --> 34:55.791
So Wesson killed himself.
What the hell is going on here?

34:57.791 --> 35:01.708
Mr. Bergin, I'm Agent Max Williams.
This is Agent Greer.

35:02.416 --> 35:06.416
Any chance either of you guys could…
get me another apple juice?

35:09.458 --> 35:12.707
I had a look at your sheet.
You're quite the overachiever.

35:12.708 --> 35:15.625
Miscarriages of justice,
every single one of them.

35:16.458 --> 35:17.458
In fact, I'm a…

35:18.541 --> 35:19.790
upstanding citizen.

35:19.791 --> 35:20.915
Hmm.

35:20.916 --> 35:24.415
Who shot and killed a 70-year-old woman
in broad daylight?

35:24.416 --> 35:26.124
That was Burroughs.

35:26.125 --> 35:29.582
He shoots Hilde,
he tortures and kidnaps me,

35:29.583 --> 35:31.499
and I'm the one that's cuffed to a bed.

35:31.500 --> 35:33.332
Great job. Great job.

35:33.333 --> 35:35.291
Two things wrong with your story.

35:35.958 --> 35:37.999
One, we know you shot yourself.

35:38.000 --> 35:39.832
We got that on video.

35:39.833 --> 35:43.208
And two, we retrieved your gun
from the construction site.

35:43.833 --> 35:45.915
So if the bullet
that the doctor pulled from your gut

35:45.916 --> 35:48.457
matches the one in Hilde's chest,
we got you on murder.

35:48.458 --> 35:49.790
You don't have shit.

35:49.791 --> 35:51.666
Wanna bet your life on that, buddy?

35:52.250 --> 35:54.499
Because see, this is federal, which means,

35:54.500 --> 35:58.165
unless we take it off,
death penalty's on the table.

35:58.166 --> 35:59.332
It was Burroughs.

35:59.333 --> 36:01.958
I'm telling you, the guy's insane.
He thinks his son is alive.

36:05.333 --> 36:07.540
He said that?
He said he thinks his son's alive?

36:07.541 --> 36:10.290
Yeah, the one he beat to death
with a baseball bat.

36:10.291 --> 36:12.749
That's what I'm saying.
The guy's got a screw loose.

36:12.750 --> 36:14.625
What about Hilde Winslow?
Why'd she call you?

36:15.958 --> 36:17.708
Because she was scared of Burroughs.

36:18.291 --> 36:21.250
But why did she call you?

36:27.416 --> 36:28.416
All right.

36:29.125 --> 36:31.208
I can phrase this another way. So…

36:34.458 --> 36:36.666
What's Nicky Fisher
got to do with all this?

36:40.250 --> 36:42.083
Forget the apple juice.

36:43.083 --> 36:45.875
Why don't you just go get me my lawyer?

36:51.208 --> 36:55.290
Hey, I ordered some cavatelli
from La Morra. Should be here in a minute.

36:55.291 --> 36:56.166
Okay.

37:17.291 --> 37:19.540
Cheryl. It's Lenny Burroughs.

37:19.541 --> 37:23.416
I have some new information about why
Ronald might have lied about that night.

37:29.250 --> 37:31.999
Echoing your voice

37:32.000 --> 37:36.582
Just like the ringing in my ear

37:36.583 --> 37:38.624
Never thought I'd be going home.

37:38.625 --> 37:39.749
My favorite dreams…

37:39.750 --> 37:41.249
Nervous about seeing your dad?

37:41.250 --> 37:43.500
…still wash ashore

37:46.166 --> 37:48.249
He never said it,
but I could tell by his eyes at the trial

37:48.250 --> 37:49.291
that he thought I did it.

37:52.250 --> 37:53.666
We're gonna make things right.

37:54.583 --> 37:55.750
For both of you.

37:58.208 --> 37:59.458
For all of us.

38:11.708 --> 38:15.124
You always were the one

38:15.125 --> 38:17.458
To show me how…

38:20.125 --> 38:21.457
Hello, Mother, how are you?

38:21.458 --> 38:25.207
I'm near the Commonwealth.
I thought I'd drop by and say hello.

38:25.208 --> 38:27.207
Oh, I would love that,
but I'm not home right now.

38:27.208 --> 38:28.915
How unfortunate.

38:28.916 --> 38:30.582
Yeah, something came up.

38:30.583 --> 38:34.291
- I had to leave town for the evening.
- Oh, well, it must be very important.

38:37.250 --> 38:40.999
- What can I do for you, Mother?
- I'll come by the office tomorrow morning.

38:41.000 --> 38:42.583
We can talk about it then.

38:43.416 --> 38:44.583
Good night, dear.

38:45.958 --> 38:55.040
You make this all go away

38:55.041 --> 38:59.124
I'm down to just one thing

38:59.125 --> 39:03.500
And I'm starting to scare myself

39:18.791 --> 39:27.832
You make this all go away

39:27.833 --> 39:31.957
I'm down to just one thing

39:31.958 --> 39:34.749
And I'm starting to scare myself

39:34.750 --> 39:36.499
Holy shit.

39:36.500 --> 39:45.457
You make this all go away

39:45.458 --> 39:48.541
I just want something

39:49.916 --> 39:52.624
I just want something

39:52.625 --> 39:55.625
I can never have

39:57.708 --> 40:03.333
Everywhere I look, you're all I see

40:05.666 --> 40:10.290
Just a fading fucking reminder

40:10.291 --> 40:13.707
Of who I used to be

40:13.708 --> 40:15.999
Come on and tell me

40:16.000 --> 40:24.915
You make this all go away

40:24.916 --> 40:29.249
I'm down to just one thing

40:29.250 --> 40:33.291
And I'm starting to scare myself

40:33.833 --> 40:38.207
You make this all go away

40:38.208 --> 40:42.665
You make it all go away

40:42.666 --> 40:45.541
I just want something

40:47.125 --> 40:49.957
I just want something

40:49.958 --> 40:53.625
I can never have

40:55.750 --> 40:58.832
I just want something

40:58.833 --> 41:03.750
I can never have
